{"text": "= James Peet\n\nPROFILE: I ama school leader who values cultural and intellectual diversity and is driven to provide high\nquality learning experiences for all students. I strive to create mission driven, data informed and solution-\noriented systems of change. By working together, I believe schools and communities can create safe and healthy\nenvironments that foster social emotional and intellectual development for children.\n\nCell:\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n1017-Present\n\nHernandez Middle School-Chicago, Illinois Jul\nAssistant Principal\n\nLeadership Development\n\u00a9 Co-Lead Instructional Leadership Team\n\u2018\u00a9 Created and successfully implemented a cycle of professional learning around targeting teacher\npractices of increasing Agency, Authority, and Identity in the classroom\n\u2018\u00a9 Supported leadership development of ILT members - Created professional development around\ncompleting a walkthrough of the building; Created walkthrough protocols; Calibrated scores\nwith ILT members; Debriefed data to determine problems of practice\n* Created and Provided a Professional Development Series around Analyzing and Using Data\n(\u00a9 Used flex day PD\u2019s to identify students underperforming on the NWEA or in class, based on data\nmeasures\n* Led Math Team\n\u2018\u00a9 Focused on alignment of standards - Reviewed yearly scope and sequence and began planning\nstages on redesigning pacing\n\u00a9 Coached teachers in implementing practices resulting in an increase of student centered learning\n* Co-Led CIWP Team During Writing Process\n\u2018\u00a9 Developed the sequence of activities that guided the CIWP writing team to on-time completion\nof the current iteration of the CIWP\n\nFamily and Community Outreach\n\u00a9 Authored Grants\n\u2018\u00a9 Wrote and received a grant to partner with the Community School\u2019s Initiative, impacting 400\nstudents who have signed up for at least one after school program\n\u2018\u00a9 Wrote and received a grant to partner with the Dyson Foundation - Brought the Design, Build,\nTest Club to Hernandez\n* Developed Schoo! Partnerships\n\u2018\u00a9 Brought Becoming a Man to Hernandez to support our 7\" and 8\" grade boys in their social\nemotional development\n\u00a9 Designed and Implemented after School Events for Parents and Community\n\u2018\u00a9 Partnered in organizing school events such as report card pick-up, school play, 6\"-8\" grade\norientations, press conferences, ete.\n\nInstructional Evaluation and Support\n* REACH Evaluation\n\u2018\u00a9 Successfillly completed reach evaluation for 1/3\" of the teachers in Hernandez",
